# Haskell backend (external, protocol 2) — Bazel migration Phase 3.
#
# The emitter runs *out of process* over the emit protocol: `sudoc build
# --target hs --external <manifest>` spawns `runghc Emit.hs` (cwd = this dir),
# so the codegen action needs the manifest, the emitter (Emit.hs), its import
# SudoJson.hs, and SudoRt.hs (read via `readFile "SudoRt.hs"` and emitted into
# the generated tree as the runtime). All four must be siblings at emit time.
#
# Unlike the in-tree backends, hs codegen shells out to the host GHC, so its
# lockstep codegen action is a no-sandbox `local` action inheriting host PATH
# (spec §8 Phase 3 "system-GHC no-sandbox leaf"). Under the Phase-3 fallback the
# manifest IS the hs registration mechanism (`--external` / discovery), so it
# stays in-tree; it is retired when Phase 5's `sudo_external_backend` rule
# replaces it. (cargo, and its manifest discovery, is already gone.)

filegroup(
    name = "emitter",
    srcs = [
        "Emit.hs",
        "SudoJson.hs",
        "SudoRt.hs",
        "hs.sudoc-backend.json",
    ],
    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
)
